 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Chef Barinov asks if their upcoming wedding was also a cover, and Elena assures him her love is real. She gives him five minutes to say goodbye to his daughter Katya and tells him to shave off his famous mustache.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "А как же наша свадьба?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Это тоже было твоё прикрытие?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Нет, я действительно тебя люблю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Поэтому я помогаю тебе сбежать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Возьми, это твой новый паспорт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Ты должен срочно покинуть страну.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "По ветке доберёшься до аэропорта.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Там в номере связаны люди.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Не волнуйся, я позабочусь о них.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Мне надо попрощаться с Катей.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Хорошо, даю тебе немного времени.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "И не забудь сбрить усы.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "А как же наша свадьба?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And what about our wedding?' In Russian, the idea of 'and' flows naturally into 'wedding' without extra filler words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Это тоже было твоё прикрытие?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Was that also your cover story?' Notice how Russian expresses 'this' and 'cover story' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Elena answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Нет, я действительно тебя люблю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, I truly love you.' Elena anchors the line on 'no', while 'like' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Поэтому я помогаю тебе сбежать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'That is why I am helping you escape.' The grammar packs 'therefore' and 'to escape' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Возьми, это твой новый паспорт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Take this, it is your new passport.' Notice how Russian expresses 'take' and 'passport' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Ты должен срочно покинуть страну.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You must leave the country urgently.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'you' before landing on 'country'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "По ветке доберёшься до аэропорта.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Along the line you will reach the airport.' The meaning hinges on 'according to' working together with 'airport' in spoken Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Там в номере связаны люди.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'People are tied up in the room over there.' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'there' and 'number' in a few short words. Elena answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Не волнуйся, я позабочусь о них.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Do not worry, I will take care of them.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'not' before landing on 'them'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Мне надо попрощаться с Катей.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I need to say goodbye to Katya.' In Russian, the idea of 'to me' flows naturally into 'with' without extra filler words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Хорошо, даю тебе немного времени.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Alright, I give you a little time.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'well' and finishing on 'time'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "И не забудь сбрить усы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
